The Waterline Restaurant at Keppel Bay Marina invites applications for an experienced Chef.
Job Types: Full-time, Permanent
Salary: $79423.00 - $80,000.00 per year + Super
Job Address: 1 Waterline Way, Rosslyn QLD 4703
Aside from the excellent view, we offer a modern contemporary menu with Asian influences seven days a week.
Key responsibilities will include:
Cooking and preparing various menus from Breakfast to Evening dining;
Adhering to recipes and procedures;
Discussing formal preparation issues with Managers, Dieticians and Kitchen & Waiting staff;
Selecting and training staff;
Maintaining restaurant plating and cooking standards; and
Working 38 hours/week.
Required skills and attributes:
A career-focused progression as a Chef with a passion for food;
Ability to be adaptable and work various shifts across a 7-day operation;
Previous experience in a high volume a la carte restaurant environment;
Attention to detail;
Strong work ethic;
Excellent communication skills;
As you are working in an Open Kitchen, Chef must have a good kitchen temperament and personal presentation;
Being a team member;
Previous experience in modern Asian/Australian cuisine is preferred.
A great lifestyle awaits in a coastal town with access to beautiful National Parks, beaches, the Keppel Islands, and the Southern Great Barrier reef.
Schedule:
8 hour shift

Summary of role requirements:
Looking for candidates available to work on weekdays, Saturdays and Sundays
2-3 years of relevant work experience required for this role
Job Types: Permanent, Full-time

Schedule:
8 hour shift
Weekend availability
Work Authorisation:
Australia (Preferred)
Work Location: In person

DAIRY CATTLE FARM OPERATOR
Location: Riverslea, VIC 3860 
Tenure: Full-time, Permanent
Comprehensive salary package from $71,481 pa (plus superannuation)

Required Skills and Experience: 
•	At least an AQF certificate II or III in Agriculture (or equivalent)
•	At least one (1) year of recent and relevant work experience

Position Summary:

On behalf of our client, Global Skilled Employment Services is looking for a skilled and experienced Dairy Cattle Farm Operator who can use their knowledge and skills to perform set procedures such as milking and attending to livestock, haymaking, and fencing, then applies the knowledge and skills to multiple operations involving basic levels of problem solving and decision making and has an appreciation of the overall processes involved in a dairy farm.

This is a full-time position which may involve weekend or public holidays work and some unplanned hours of work where the need arises (paid accordingly).

Duties and responsibilities: 

•	Operate milking plant and equipment; 
•	Identify and report equipment not operating normally; 
•	Work co-operatively as part of a team;
•	Read and record instrument information i.e. Milk vat temperatures and cow numbers; and 
•	Understands the principles of safe working; 
•	Undertake multiple functions, produce a quality outcome e.g. Farm machinery; 
•	Maintain machinery, undertake adjustments and size changes; 
•	Solve problems and make decisions within given guidelines; 
•	Know general scientific terminology and assist with processes such as machine repair, artificial insemination, fertiliser mix design etc.; 
•	Operate standard measuring equipment 
•	Operate computerised systems using menu options 
•	Contribute to the team in a specific role, providing input and assisting other team members; and 
•	Work at times without supervision 


Qualified applicants may apply online.

